  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result is config_027 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) at 0.535 acc. We've established that concat≈weighted fusion and pca≈scvi RNA encoder (differences <0.5%), and that image alone is weak (0.227) but adds ~5% in multimodal. The entire multiprofile dimension remains completely untested—this is the largest source of uncertainty. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile (with avgpool aggregation) improve over the best singleprofile result, holding RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion constant? config_049 is the minimal, direct extension of config_027 into multiprofile space (same pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat; only profile setting and aggregation change, and aggregation is a necessary consequence of multiprofile). Why best use of budget: It isolates the single most important unexplored design axis (multiprofile vs singleprofile) with the simplest aggregation, avoiding confounds from simultaneously changing encoder or fusion. A positive result would justify further investment in multiprofile variants (transformer aggregation, other encoders); a negative result would redirect budget toward other axes (image encoder choice, scgpt)."
}

